<item><title>Zimbabwe urged to weigh mining bill carefully before passage</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/zimbabwe-urged-to-weigh-mining-bill-carefully-before-passage-1bb970/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/zimbabwe-urged-to-weigh-mining-bill-carefully-before-passage-1bb970/</guid><category>Zimbabwe</category><description>The Zimbabwe Independent says the 1961 Mines and Minerals Act no longer reflects the mining industry, while mining remains important to the economy.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:03:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zw.jpg" length="34422" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Zimbabwe High Court orders ZIMRA to refund unlawful duty on US$130,000 car</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/zimbabwe-high-court-orders-zimra-to-refund-unlawful-duty-on-9f375a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/zimbabwe-high-court-orders-zimra-to-refund-unlawful-duty-on-9f375a/</guid><category>Zimbabwe</category><description>The court ruled the returning resident met the ownership test and gave the revenue authority 30 days to calculate any refund due.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:39:07 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zw.jpg" length="34422" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Ncube proposes lower IMTT rates in 2027 budget</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/ncube-proposes-lower-imtt-rates-in-2027-budget-e75728/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/ncube-proposes-lower-imtt-rates-in-2027-budget-e75728/</guid><category>Zimbabwe</category><description>The proposal cuts the charge on ZiG transactions from 1,5% to 1,25% and on foreign currency transactions from 2% to 1,75%.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:14:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/ncube-proposes-lower-imtt-rates-in-2027-budget-e75728/share.jpg" length="39303" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/zw/ncube-proposes-lower-imtt-rates-in-2027-budget-e75728/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
